jordan_customer: Hey team — hitting a toolcall error in prod after migrating to the new SDK. Calls to /v1/tools/invoke are returning a schema validation failure. Sample error: "ValidationError: additionalProperties not allowed: meta". Any ideas?

alice_support: Hi @jordan_customer, thanks for reporting — can you paste the request body (redact secrets) and the exact error payload from the API response? Also which SDK version?

jordan_customer: SDK v2.8.1. Here's the request we send:```json
{
  "tool": "order-fulfill",
  "args": {
    "order_id": 12345,
    "items": [ { "sku": "A-1", "qty": 2 } ],
    "meta": { "source": "mobile" }
  },
  "session_id": 98765
}
```And the API returns:```json
{
  "error": {
    "type": "schema.validation_error",
    "message": "additionalProperties: meta at /args",
    "code": "invalid_toolcall_payload"
  }
}
```

alice_support: Ok — two quick questions: (1) Is order_id supposed to be a string in the tool schema? (2) Can you share the tool's declared JSON schema (the one registered with the model) for args?

jordan_customer: The tool schema we registered is the one our infra team pushed last week — copied below:```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "order_id": { "type": "string" },
    "items": { "type": "array" },
    "notes": { "type": "string" }
  },
  "required": ["order_id", "items"],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```Note: we recently started sending session_id at top level and a meta map under args for tracing.

sam_engineer: Thanks — looks like two issues: 1) order_id is declared as string, but you're sending a number (12345) — that will trigger a type mismatch. 2) The schema sets additionalProperties: false so any arg not listed (meta) will be rejected. Both would surface as schema validation errors in the same response or similar ones depending on validator.

sam_engineer: Quick repro I ran locally replicating your payload (using the registered schema) -> validator output:```json
[
  {"keyword":"type","dataPath":".args.order_id","message":"should be string"},
  {"keyword":"additionalProperties","dataPath":".args","message":"additional property \"meta\" is not allowed"}
]
```

jordan_customer: Oof, that explains it. We thought order_id could be numeric. Is there a recommended remediation path without changing the tool schema?

alice_support: Two options: (A) Convert order_id to string in your client before calling (quick fix). (B) If you control the tool schema and want to accept numbers, update the schema to allow both types: e.g., "order_id": { "anyOf": [{"type":"string"},{"type":"integer"}] }. Also either remove `additionalProperties:false` or add `meta` to `properties` if you want to keep strict mode.

jordan_customer: We'll try (A) for now. For longer term we'll likely add meta to properties. One more thing: we sometimes pass session_id as an int at top-level — does the top-level envelope have a schema?

sam_engineer: The invocation envelope does have server-side validation for top-level fields depending on your org's tool registration. Right now session_id isn't documented as required, but if your contract expects a string you should stringify it. If you want, paste the exact top-level schema and we can advise changes.

jordan_customer: Repro steps I used for quick test:```bash
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.example/v1/tools/invoke \n  -H 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' \n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \n  -d '{"tool":"order-fulfill","args":{"order_id":12345,"items":[{"sku":"A-1","qty":2}],"meta":{"source":"mobile"}},"session_id":98765}'
```Response: the same schema.validation_error with both messages.

alice_support: Thanks — that's perfect. I'll mark a follow-up ticket to add a short KB entry for common schema pitfalls (type mismatch + additionalProperties). For now set order_id to string and either drop meta or add it to the schema.

repro_bot: Note saved to ticket #SUP-1987: "schema errors on toolcall due to order_id type and extra meta field" :spiral_note_pad:

jordan_customer: Fixed on our side by casting order_id to string and adding meta to the tool schema. Re-tested — no validation errors and tool executes. Thanks all :thumbsup:

alice_support: Great to hear — closing the thread. If you hit anything else ping us and include the payload + schema snippets.
